> import ode
> help ode.solve
solve(f, y0, tspan; method = "rk45", rtol = 1e-6, atol = 1e-9, t_eval = nothing, events = nothing, terminal = false, direction = 0, names = nothing, max_step = nothing, first_step = nothing, max_steps = 100000)
  Solves y' = f(t, y) from tspan[1] to tspan[2] with y(tspan[1]) = y0.
  method is "rk45" (explicit, the default) or "bdf" (stiff, CVODE). Returns a
  record with t, y (one column per time), names, status ("success" or
  "event"), t_events, y_events, nfev, nsteps and at(t) for dense output.
> import graphics
> help graphics
module graphics
  Renders a scene (a record of drawing items) to PNG, SVG or PDF through Skia.
  exports: save, text_width
> help graphics.save
save(scene, path)
  Renders a scene to a .png, .svg or .pdf file
> import plot
> help plot.line
line(x, y; label = nothing, color = nothing, width = 1.5, style = "-", marker = nothing, marker_size = 5.0)
  Adds a line through the points (x[k], y[k]). Keywords: label, color,
  width (points), style ("-", "--", ":" or "-.") and marker (a marker shape
  drawn at each point, with marker_size).
